From 865247f71f37b2699241cb6200fd54b0ec70a76e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SendHelpOrGG <343593581+SendHelpOrGG@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:24:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Port fetch_via_savefree as the resolver's last resort

Ports fetch_via_savefree, decode_hunter_js and is_video_cdn_url from the
original server.py into SaveFreeClient:

- POSTs the post URL to save-free.net/api/ajaxSearch as the browser does
  (form body q/t/lang/v, save-free origin and referer)
- decodes the Hunter-encoded JS response (eval(function(p,a,c,k,e,d))
  with the charset-index replacement loop) into the innerHTML markup,
  falling back to parsing the body directly when it is not encoded
- unwraps base64url token= download links into real CDN URLs
- reads slides out of each <li>: first <option> wins, anchor and
  thumbnail are fallbacks; a video keeps the thumbnail as poster and the
  download URL as videoUrl
- detects video from icon-dlvideo / Download Video / .mp4 / /o1/v/t /
  the efg base64 marker, exactly like the original

InstagramResolver asks for it only when the direct result cannot stand
on its own: no cover (summary), no slides or OG-only source, or a video
slide without a playable URL. More slides wins, equal counts merge slide
by slide, and the ask is capped at 6 s so an opened post stays inside the
web layer's 12 s budget.

Verified against the Python original: the decoder matches on 824
generated payloads, and the item parser returns byte-identical slides
for a fixture covering option/anchor/thumbnail sources, JWT unwrapping
and all four video signals.

Also ignores ig_session.json and friends: session cookies must never be
committed.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
